    {
      "title": "Labor Organization Annual Financial Reports",
      "type": "Rule",
      "abstract": "The Department of Labor (Department) publishes this combined final rule to its regulations to improve its LM Labor Organization Annual Financial Reports by establishing a longer LM form for the largest labor organizations (Form LM-2 Long Form), revising a slightly shorter form for most labor organizations at and above the $350,000 threshold (Form LM-2), making a parallel revision to Form LM-3, and updating reporting thresholds for Forms LM-3 and LM-4 to promote financial integrity and transparency. The final rule applies prospectively under section 208 of the Labor-Management Reporting and Disclosure Act of 1959 (LMRDA).",
      "html_url": "https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/06/01/2026-10849/labor-organization-annual-financial-reports",
